{title: Holy, Holy, Holy}
{lyricist: Reginald Heber, 1826}
{composer: NICAEA, John B. Dykes, 1861}
{copyright: Public domain}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 88}

{start_of_verse}
[Eb]Holy, holy, [Cm]holy! [Ab]Lord God Al[Eb]mighty!
[Eb]Early in the [Bb]morning our [Cm]song shall [F]rise to [Bb]Thee;
[Eb]Holy, holy, [Cm]holy! [Ab]merciful and [Eb]mighty!
[Ab]God in three [Eb]Per[Cm]sons, [Eb/Bb]bless[Bb]ed [Eb]Trinity!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[Eb]Holy, holy, [Cm]holy! [Ab]All the saints a[Eb]dore Thee,
[Eb]Casting down their [Bb]golden crowns a[Cm]round the [F]glassy [Bb]sea;
[Eb]Cherubim and [Cm]seraphim [Ab]falling down be[Eb]fore Thee,
[Ab]Which wert, and [Eb]art, and [Cm]ever[Eb/Bb]more [Bb]shalt [Eb]be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[Eb]Holy, holy, [Cm]holy! [Ab]though the darkness [Eb]hide Thee,
[Eb]Though the eye of [Bb]sinful man Thy [Cm]glory [F]may not [Bb]see;
[Eb]Only Thou art [Cm]holy; [Ab]there is none be[Eb]side Thee,
[Ab]Perfect in [Eb]power, in [Cm]love, and [Eb/Bb]pu[Bb]ri[Eb]ty.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[Eb]Holy, holy, [Cm]holy! [Ab]Lord God Al[Eb]mighty!
[Eb]All Thy works shall [Bb]praise Thy Name, in [Cm]earth, and [F]sky, and [Bb]sea;
[Eb]Holy, holy, [Cm]holy! [Ab]merciful and [Eb]mighty!
[Ab]God in three [Eb]Per[Cm]sons, [Eb/Bb]bless[Bb]ed [Eb]Trinity!
{end_of_verse}
